    "text": "Here's the implementation of the function `any_int`:\n\n```python\ndef any_int(x, y, z):\n```\n\nNow, let's complete the function.\n:\n\n```\ntry:\n    # Check if all are integers (instance)\n    # return (isinstance(int(x, int) and isinstance(y, int) and isinstance(z, int))\n    \n    # Check if any number is equal to the sum of the other two\n    return (x == y + z or y == x + z or z == x + y)\nexcept TypeError:\n    return False\n```\n\nThis function first checks if all three numbers are integers. If so, it then checks if any of the numbers is equal to the sum of the other two. If it meets these conditions, it returns `True`; otherwise, it returns `False`. If the numbers are not integers, the function returns `False` immediately.",
